{"id":"Q_CH12_001","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Choosing appropriate units","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"To measure the perimeter of a classroom, which of the following units is suitable?","questionLatex":"\\text{Suitable unit for classroom perimeter:}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"litre"},{"id":"B","text":"metre"},{"id":"C","text":"kilogram"},{"id":"D","text":"any of these"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["Perimeter means the distance around something. Which unit measures distance?","Litre measures liquids, kilogram measures weight. What measures length?","Metre is the unit for measuring length and distance."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Perimeter = total length around a shape.","latex":"\\text{Perimeter} = \\text{length measurement}"},{"step":2,"text":"Litre = capacity/volume, Kilogram = mass/weight, Metre = length.","latex":"\\text{Length} \\rightarrow \\text{metre (m)}"},{"step":3,"text":"So metre is the suitable unit.","latex":"\\boxed{\\text{metre}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Litre measures capacity (liquids), not length","B":"","C":"Kilogram measures mass/weight, not length","D":"Only metre measures length — these units are not interchangeable"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_002","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Currency conversion","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"If 1 American dollar = 40 Indian rupees, how many American dollars will you get in exchange of 100 Indian rupees?","questionLatex":"1 \\text{ dollar} = ₹40. \\quad ₹100 = ? \\text{ dollars}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"2.5"},{"id":"B","text":"0.04"},{"id":"C","text":"2.25"},{"id":"D","text":"4000"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["If 1 dollar = 40 rupees, then to find how many dollars 100 rupees makes, divide!","Number of dollars = 100 ÷ 40","100 ÷ 40 = 2.5 dollars"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 dollar = 40 rupees. We have 100 rupees.","latex":"1 \\text{ dollar} = ₹40"},{"step":2,"text":"Divide rupees by the exchange rate.","latex":"100 \\div 40 = 2.5"},{"step":3,"text":"So 100 rupees = 2.5 dollars","latex":"\\boxed{₹100 = 2.5 \\text{ dollars}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Divided 1 by 40 (found value of 1 rupee in dollars, not 100 rupees)","C":"Calculation error","D":"Multiplied 100 × 40 instead of dividing"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_003","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Metric prefix conversion","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"To convert decametre to decimetre:","questionLatex":"\\text{decametre} \\rightarrow \\text{decimetre: }","options":[{"id":"A","text":"multiply by 100"},{"id":"B","text":"divide by 100"},{"id":"C","text":"divide by 1000"},{"id":"D","text":"multiply by 10"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["Use the metric ladder: Kilo-Hecto-Deca-UNIT-Deci-Centi-Milli. Count the steps!","Deca is 2 steps above Deci. Moving down the ladder means multiplying by 10 each step.","2 steps down = multiply by 10 × 10 = 100"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Place on the metric ladder: Deca is above the unit, Deci is below.","latex":"\\text{Deca} \\xrightarrow{\\times 10} \\text{Unit} \\xrightarrow{\\times 10} \\text{Deci}"},{"step":2,"text":"Deca to Deci = 2 steps down = multiply by 10 × 10.","latex":"10 \\times 10 = 100"},{"step":3,"text":"So multiply by 100.","latex":"\\boxed{\\text{multiply by } 100}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Divided instead of multiplied (went up the ladder instead of down)","C":"Counted 3 steps instead of 2","D":"Only counted 1 step"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_004","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Metric relationship (1/100)","difficulty":"Hard","questionText":"In which of the following pairs is one unit 1/100 times the other?","questionLatex":"\\text{Which pair has a } \\frac{1}{100} \\text{ relationship?}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"metre & kilometre"},{"id":"B","text":"centilitre & litre"},{"id":"C","text":"gram & decagram"},{"id":"D","text":"kilogram & tonne"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["1/100 means one unit is 100 times smaller than the other. Which prefix means 1/100?","'Centi' means 1/100. So centilitre = 1/100 of a litre!","1 centilitre = 1/100 litre. That's the 1/100 relationship."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"We need a pair where one is exactly 1/100 of the other.","latex":"\\frac{1}{100} \\text{ relationship}"},{"step":2,"text":"Check each: metre = 1/1000 km (not 1/100). Gram = 1/10 decagram (not 1/100). Kg = 1/1000 tonne (not 1/100).","latex":"\\text{m} = \\frac{1}{1000} \\text{km} \\quad \\text{g} = \\frac{1}{10} \\text{Dg}"},{"step":3,"text":"Centilitre = 1/100 litre. 'Centi' literally means hundredth!","latex":"\\boxed{1 \\text{ cl} = \\frac{1}{100} \\text{ l}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Metre is 1/1000 of a kilometre, not 1/100","B":"","C":"Gram is 1/10 of a decagram, not 1/100","D":"Kilogram is 1/1000 of a tonne, not 1/100"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_005","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Capacity conversion (ml to l)","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"125 ml = _______ l","questionLatex":"125 \\text{ ml} = ? \\text{ l}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"1/125"},{"id":"B","text":"5/4"},{"id":"C","text":"1.25"},{"id":"D","text":"1/8"}],"correctAnswer":"D","hints":["1 litre = 1000 ml. To convert ml to litres, divide by 1000.","125 ÷ 1000 = 0.125. Now simplify 0.125 as a fraction.","0.125 = 125/1000 = 1/8"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert ml to litres: divide by 1000.","latex":"125 \\div 1000 = 0.125 \\text{ l}"},{"step":2,"text":"Express as a fraction: 125/1000.","latex":"\\frac{125}{1000}"},{"step":3,"text":"Simplify: divide both by 125.","latex":"\\frac{125 \\div 125}{1000 \\div 125} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Wrote 1/125 instead of 125/1000","B":"Confused with 1250 ml = 5/4 l","C":"Divided by 100 instead of 1000","D":""},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_006","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mass conversion (kg to g)","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"37.02 kg = ?","questionLatex":"37.02 \\text{ kg} = ?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"3702 g"},{"id":"B","text":"37 2/100 g"},{"id":"C","text":"37 kg 2 g"},{"id":"D","text":"37 kg 20 g"}],"correctAnswer":"D","hints":["Think about what 0.02 kg means in grams. 1 kg = 1000 g.","0.02 kg = 0.02 × 1000 = 20 g. So 37.02 kg = 37 kg and 20 g.","37 kg 20 g is the correct way to express it."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Split: 37.02 kg = 37 kg + 0.02 kg","latex":"37.02 = 37 + 0.02"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert 0.02 kg to grams: 0.02 × 1000 = 20 g","latex":"0.02 \\times 1000 = 20 \\text{ g}"},{"step":3,"text":"So 37.02 kg = 37 kg 20 g","latex":"\\boxed{37 \\text{ kg } 20 \\text{ g}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Converted ALL to grams (37.02 × 1000 = 37020 g, not 3702 g — this answer is also wrong)","B":"Wrote it as a mixed fraction, not a measurement","C":"Thought 0.02 kg = 2 g (forgot to multiply by 1000)","D":""},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_007","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Score, dozen, gross","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"How many articles make 0.3 score?","questionLatex":"0.3 \\text{ score} = ? \\text{ articles}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"3"},{"id":"B","text":"5"},{"id":"C","text":"6"},{"id":"D","text":"30"}],"correctAnswer":"C","hints":["First, how many articles are in 1 score?","1 score = 20 articles. So 0.3 score = 0.3 × 20.","0.3 × 20 = 6 articles"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 score = 20 articles","latex":"1 \\text{ score} = 20 \\text{ articles}"},{"step":2,"text":"0.3 score = 0.3 × 20","latex":"0.3 \\times 20 = 6"},{"step":3,"text":"So 0.3 score = 6 articles","latex":"\\boxed{6 \\text{ articles}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Thought 1 score = 10 articles","B":"Thought 1 score = 16.67 articles","C":"","D":"Thought 0.3 score means 30 (ignored the decimal)"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_008","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Score, dozen, gross","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"How many gross make a dozen?","questionLatex":"? \\text{ gross} = 1 \\text{ dozen}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"1/12"},{"id":"B","text":"12"},{"id":"C","text":"144"},{"id":"D","text":"0.12"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["1 gross = 12 dozens = 144 articles. 1 dozen = 12 articles.","We need: how many gross = 1 dozen? Since 1 gross = 12 dozens...","1 dozen = 1/12 of a gross."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 gross = 12 dozens = 144 articles","latex":"1 \\text{ gross} = 12 \\text{ dozens}"},{"step":2,"text":"So 1 dozen = 1/12 gross","latex":"1 \\text{ dozen} = \\frac{1}{12} \\text{ gross}"},{"step":3,"text":"1/12 gross make a dozen.","latex":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{12}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"This is how many dozens make a gross (reversed the question)","C":"This is how many articles make a gross","D":"Confused with decimal conversion"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_009","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mixed unit addition","difficulty":"Hard","questionText":"4 km + 40 m + 400 cm = how many metres?","questionLatex":"4 \\text{ km} + 40 \\text{ m} + 400 \\text{ cm} = ? \\text{ metres}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"4044"},{"id":"B","text":"40404"},{"id":"C","text":"4.404"},{"id":"D","text":"4044.0"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["Convert everything to metres first. 1 km = ? m and 1 cm = ? m","4 km = 4000 m. 400 cm = 4 m. Now add all three.","4000 + 40 + 4 = 4044 metres"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert km to m: 4 km = 4 × 1000 = 4000 m","latex":"4 \\text{ km} = 4000 \\text{ m}"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert cm to m: 400 cm = 400 ÷ 100 = 4 m","latex":"400 \\text{ cm} = 4 \\text{ m}"},{"step":3,"text":"Add: 4000 + 40 + 4 = 4044 m","latex":"\\boxed{4000 + 40 + 4 = 4044 \\text{ m}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Didn't convert properly — just joined the numbers","C":"Converted to km instead of metres","D":"Same as A but with unnecessary decimal — both would be accepted"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_010","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Length word problem with division","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"How many pieces each of 3 cm can be cut from a ribbon that is 6.9 metres long?","questionLatex":"\\text{Ribbon} = 6.9 \\text{ m}, \\text{ piece} = 3 \\text{ cm}. \\text{ How many pieces?}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"23"},{"id":"B","text":"230"},{"id":"C","text":"2.3"},{"id":"D","text":"3.9"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["The ribbon is in metres but pieces are in cm. Convert to the same unit first!","6.9 m = 6.9 × 100 = 690 cm. Now divide by 3 cm.","690 ÷ 3 = 230 pieces"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert ribbon to cm: 6.9 m = 690 cm","latex":"6.9 \\times 100 = 690 \\text{ cm}"},{"step":2,"text":"Divide by piece length: 690 ÷ 3","latex":"690 \\div 3 = 230"},{"step":3,"text":"230 pieces can be cut.","latex":"\\boxed{230 \\text{ pieces}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Divided 6.9 ÷ 0.03 incorrectly, or divided 69 ÷ 3","B":"","C":"Divided 6.9 ÷ 3 without converting units","D":"Subtracted instead of dividing"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
