{"id":"Q_CH12_011","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Capacity word problem","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"If one bottle can hold 125 ml of oil, how many such bottles are needed to fill 2.5 litres of oil?","questionLatex":"\\text{Bottle} = 125 \\text{ ml}. \\text{ Total} = 2.5 \\text{ l}. \\text{ Bottles} = ?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"100"},{"id":"B","text":"25"},{"id":"C","text":"200"},{"id":"D","text":"20"}],"correctAnswer":"D","hints":["Convert litres to ml first. 1 litre = 1000 ml.","2.5 litres = 2500 ml. Now divide by 125 ml per bottle.","2500 ÷ 125 = 20 bottles"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert: 2.5 l = 2500 ml","latex":"2.5 \\times 1000 = 2500 \\text{ ml}"},{"step":2,"text":"Divide: 2500 ÷ 125","latex":"2500 \\div 125 = 20"},{"step":3,"text":"20 bottles are needed.","latex":"\\boxed{20 \\text{ bottles}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Divided 2500 by 25 instead of 125","B":"Divided 2500 by 100","C":"Divided 2500 by 12.5","D":""},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_012","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Length conversion (hm to dm)","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"5 hm = _______ dm","questionLatex":"5 \\text{ hm} = ? \\text{ dm}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"500"},{"id":"B","text":"5000"},{"id":"C","text":"50"},{"id":"D","text":"50000"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["Use the metric ladder: hecto is 3 steps above deci.","Each step down = multiply by 10. So 3 steps = 10 × 10 × 10 = 1000.","5 hm × 1000 = 5000 dm"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Count steps: Hecto → Deca → Unit → Deci = 3 steps down","latex":"\\text{hm} \\xrightarrow{3 \\text{ steps}} \\text{dm}"},{"step":2,"text":"Multiply by 10³ = 1000","latex":"5 \\times 1000 = 5000"},{"step":3,"text":"5 hm = 5000 dm","latex":"\\boxed{5000 \\text{ dm}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Only counted 2 steps (multiplied by 100)","B":"","C":"Only counted 1 step (multiplied by 10)","D":"Counted 4 steps (multiplied by 10000)"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_013","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mass conversion (small to large)","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"800 gm = _______ kg","questionLatex":"800 \\text{ g} = ? \\text{ kg}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"80"},{"id":"B","text":"0.8"},{"id":"C","text":"8"},{"id":"D","text":"0.08"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["To go from grams to kilograms, we go up the metric ladder. Do we multiply or divide?","Going from smaller to larger unit = divide. 1 kg = 1000 g.","800 ÷ 1000 = 0.8 kg"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"To convert g to kg, divide by 1000.","latex":"1 \\text{ kg} = 1000 \\text{ g}"},{"step":2,"text":"800 ÷ 1000 = 0.8","latex":"\\frac{800}{1000} = 0.8"},{"step":3,"text":"800 g = 0.8 kg","latex":"\\boxed{0.8 \\text{ kg}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Divided by 10 instead of 1000","B":"","C":"Divided by 100 instead of 1000","D":"Divided by 10000 instead of 1000"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_014","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Length conversion (small to large)","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"80 m = _______ km","questionLatex":"80 \\text{ m} = ? \\text{ km}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"8"},{"id":"B","text":"0.8"},{"id":"C","text":"0.08"},{"id":"D","text":"0.008"}],"correctAnswer":"C","hints":["1 km = 1000 m. To convert m to km, divide by 1000.","80 ÷ 1000 = ?","80 ÷ 1000 = 0.08 km"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 km = 1000 m. Divide m by 1000 to get km.","latex":"80 \\div 1000"},{"step":2,"text":"Move decimal 3 places left: 80 → 8.0 → 0.80 → 0.080","latex":"80 \\div 1000 = 0.08"},{"step":3,"text":"80 m = 0.08 km","latex":"\\boxed{0.08 \\text{ km}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Divided by 10 instead of 1000","B":"Divided by 100 instead of 1000","C":"","D":"Divided by 10000 instead of 1000"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_015","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Tiny mass conversion","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"5 mg = _______ g","questionLatex":"5 \\text{ mg} = ? \\text{ g}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"0.5"},{"id":"B","text":"0.05"},{"id":"C","text":"0.005"},{"id":"D","text":"5000"}],"correctAnswer":"C","hints":["1 g = 1000 mg. So to go from mg to g, divide by 1000.","5 ÷ 1000 = ?","5 ÷ 1000 = 0.005 g"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 g = 1000 mg","latex":"1 \\text{ g} = 1000 \\text{ mg}"},{"step":2,"text":"5 mg = 5 ÷ 1000 g","latex":"\\frac{5}{1000} = 0.005"},{"step":3,"text":"5 mg = 0.005 g","latex":"\\boxed{0.005 \\text{ g}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Divided by 10 instead of 1000","B":"Divided by 100 instead of 1000","C":"","D":"Multiplied by 1000 instead of dividing"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_016","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mixed length conversion","difficulty":"Hard","questionText":"3 m 7 dm = _______ cm","questionLatex":"3 \\text{ m } 7 \\text{ dm} = ? \\text{ cm}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"37"},{"id":"B","text":"370"},{"id":"C","text":"3070"},{"id":"D","text":"307"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["Convert metres and decimetres separately to cm, then add.","1 m = 100 cm. 1 dm = 10 cm.","3 m = 300 cm. 7 dm = 70 cm. Total = 300 + 70 = 370 cm."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert 3 m to cm: 3 × 100 = 300 cm","latex":"3 \\times 100 = 300 \\text{ cm}"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert 7 dm to cm: 7 × 10 = 70 cm","latex":"7 \\times 10 = 70 \\text{ cm}"},{"step":3,"text":"Add: 300 + 70 = 370 cm","latex":"\\boxed{300 + 70 = 370 \\text{ cm}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Just joined the digits 3 and 7","B":"","C":"Converted m to cm but forgot to convert dm to cm (3000 + 70)","D":"Converted 3 m to 300 cm but added 7 instead of 70"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_017","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mixed length to dm","difficulty":"Hard","questionText":"3 m 7 cm = _______ dm","questionLatex":"3 \\text{ m } 7 \\text{ cm} = ? \\text{ dm}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"3.7"},{"id":"B","text":"30.7"},{"id":"C","text":"37"},{"id":"D","text":"307"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["Convert everything to dm. 1 m = 10 dm. 1 cm = 0.1 dm.","3 m = 30 dm. 7 cm = 7 ÷ 10 = 0.7 dm.","30 + 0.7 = 30.7 dm"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert 3 m to dm: 3 × 10 = 30 dm","latex":"3 \\times 10 = 30 \\text{ dm}"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert 7 cm to dm: 7 ÷ 10 = 0.7 dm","latex":"7 \\div 10 = 0.7 \\text{ dm}"},{"step":3,"text":"Add: 30 + 0.7 = 30.7 dm","latex":"\\boxed{30.7 \\text{ dm}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Only converted m to dm, forgot to convert cm properly","B":"","C":"Just joined the digits 3 and 7","D":"Converted to cm instead of dm"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_018","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mass split (kg and g)","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"2.5 kg = _______ kg _______ g","questionLatex":"2.5 \\text{ kg} = ? \\text{ kg } ? \\text{ g}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"2 kg 5 g"},{"id":"B","text":"2 kg 50 g"},{"id":"C","text":"2 kg 500 g"},{"id":"D","text":"25 kg 0 g"}],"correctAnswer":"C","hints":["The whole number part stays as kg. The decimal part needs to be converted to grams.","0.5 kg = 0.5 × 1000 g = ?","0.5 × 1000 = 500 g. So 2.5 kg = 2 kg 500 g."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Split: 2.5 kg = 2 kg + 0.5 kg","latex":"2.5 = 2 + 0.5"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert 0.5 kg to g: 0.5 × 1000 = 500 g","latex":"0.5 \\times 1000 = 500 \\text{ g}"},{"step":3,"text":"2.5 kg = 2 kg 500 g","latex":"\\boxed{2 \\text{ kg } 500 \\text{ g}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Multiplied 0.5 by 10 instead of 1000","B":"Multiplied 0.5 by 100 instead of 1000","C":"","D":"Moved decimal wrong way entirely"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_019","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Capacity split (l and ml)","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"2.05 l = _______ l _______ ml","questionLatex":"2.05 \\text{ l} = ? \\text{ l } ? \\text{ ml}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"2 l 5 ml"},{"id":"B","text":"2 l 50 ml"},{"id":"C","text":"2 l 500 ml"},{"id":"D","text":"2 l 0.5 ml"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["2 litres stays as litres. Convert 0.05 l to ml.","1 l = 1000 ml. So 0.05 × 1000 = ?","0.05 × 1000 = 50 ml"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Split: 2.05 l = 2 l + 0.05 l","latex":"2.05 = 2 + 0.05"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert 0.05 l to ml: 0.05 × 1000 = 50 ml","latex":"0.05 \\times 1000 = 50 \\text{ ml}"},{"step":3,"text":"2.05 l = 2 l 50 ml","latex":"\\boxed{2 \\text{ l } 50 \\text{ ml}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Multiplied 0.05 by 100 instead of 1000","B":"","C":"Confused with 0.5 l = 500 ml (extra zero!)","D":"Didn't multiply by 1000"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_020","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Length split (m and cm)","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"2.05 m = _______ m _______ cm","questionLatex":"2.05 \\text{ m} = ? \\text{ m } ? \\text{ cm}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"2 m 5 cm"},{"id":"B","text":"2 m 50 cm"},{"id":"C","text":"2 m 0.5 cm"},{"id":"D","text":"20 m 5 cm"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["2 metres stays. Convert 0.05 m to cm. Remember: 1 m = 100 cm.","0.05 × 100 = ?","0.05 × 100 = 5 cm. So 2.05 m = 2 m 5 cm."],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Split: 2.05 m = 2 m + 0.05 m","latex":"2.05 = 2 + 0.05"},{"step":2,"text":"Convert 0.05 m to cm: 0.05 × 100 = 5 cm","latex":"0.05 \\times 100 = 5 \\text{ cm}"},{"step":3,"text":"2.05 m = 2 m 5 cm","latex":"\\boxed{2 \\text{ m } 5 \\text{ cm}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Multiplied by 1000 instead of 100 (confused with ml)","C":"Didn't multiply by 100","D":"Moved decimal the wrong way"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_021","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Mass conversion (quintal/tonne)","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"30 kg = _______ tonne","questionLatex":"30 \\text{ kg} = ? \\text{ tonne}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"0.3"},{"id":"B","text":"0.03"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"0.003"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["1 tonne = 1000 kg. To convert kg to tonne, divide by 1000.","30 ÷ 1000 = ?","30 ÷ 1000 = 0.03 tonne"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 tonne = 1000 kg","latex":"1 \\text{ tonne} = 1000 \\text{ kg}"},{"step":2,"text":"30 ÷ 1000 = 0.03","latex":"\\frac{30}{1000} = 0.03"},{"step":3,"text":"30 kg = 0.03 tonne","latex":"\\boxed{0.03 \\text{ tonne}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Divided by 100 instead of 1000","B":"","C":"Divided by 10 instead of 1000","D":"Divided by 10000"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_022","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Money conversion","difficulty":"Easy","questionText":"240 paise = Rs. _______","questionLatex":"240 \\text{ paise} = ₹ \\text{ ?}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"2.40"},{"id":"B","text":"24.0"},{"id":"C","text":"0.240"},{"id":"D","text":"240"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["1 rupee = 100 paise. To convert paise to rupees, divide by 100.","240 ÷ 100 = ?","240 ÷ 100 = 2.40 rupees"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 rupee = 100 paise","latex":"₹1 = 100 \\text{ paise}"},{"step":2,"text":"240 ÷ 100 = 2.40","latex":"240 \\div 100 = 2.40"},{"step":3,"text":"240 paise = Rs. 2.40","latex":"\\boxed{₹2.40}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Divided by 10 instead of 100","C":"Divided by 1000 instead of 100","D":"Didn't convert at all"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_023","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Money to paise","difficulty":"Medium","questionText":"Rs. 4.06 = _______ paise","questionLatex":"₹4.06 = ? \\text{ paise}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"46"},{"id":"B","text":"406"},{"id":"C","text":"4060"},{"id":"D","text":"4.06"}],"correctAnswer":"B","hints":["To convert rupees to paise, multiply by 100.","4.06 × 100 = ?","4.06 × 100 = 406 paise"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"1 rupee = 100 paise, so multiply by 100.","latex":"₹4.06 \\times 100"},{"step":2,"text":"Move decimal 2 places right: 4.06 → 406","latex":"4.06 \\times 100 = 406"},{"step":3,"text":"Rs. 4.06 = 406 paise","latex":"\\boxed{406 \\text{ paise}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"Dropped the 0 (only moved decimal 1 place)","B":"","C":"Multiplied by 1000 instead of 100","D":"Didn't convert at all"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_024","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Multi-step word problem","difficulty":"Hard","questionText":"A shopkeeper has 5.4 kg of rice. He sells 2 kg 750 g. How much rice is left?","questionLatex":"5.4 \\text{ kg} - 2 \\text{ kg } 750 \\text{ g} = ?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"2 kg 650 g"},{"id":"B","text":"2.65 kg"},{"id":"C","text":"3 kg 350 g"},{"id":"D","text":"2.75 kg"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["Convert both to the same format. 5.4 kg = 5 kg 400 g. 2 kg 750 g stays.","Now subtract: 5 kg 400 g - 2 kg 750 g. The grams part: 400 - 750 is negative! Borrow 1 kg.","4 kg 1400 g - 2 kg 750 g = 2 kg 650 g"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"Convert 5.4 kg: 5 kg 400 g","latex":"5.4 \\text{ kg} = 5 \\text{ kg } 400 \\text{ g}"},{"step":2,"text":"400 g < 750 g, so borrow: 4 kg 1400 g","latex":"5 \\text{ kg } 400 \\text{ g} = 4 \\text{ kg } 1400 \\text{ g}"},{"step":3,"text":"Subtract: 4 kg 1400 g - 2 kg 750 g = 2 kg 650 g","latex":"1400 - 750 = 650, \\quad 4 - 2 = 2"},{"step":4,"text":"Rice left = 2 kg 650 g","latex":"\\boxed{2 \\text{ kg } 650 \\text{ g}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Same answer as A, just in decimal (2.65 kg = 2 kg 650 g) — both correct!","C":"Added instead of subtracting","D":"Subtracted 5.4 - 2.75 but 2 kg 750 g = 2.75 kg, so this gives 2.65 not 2.75"},"source":"hand_crafted"},
{"id":"Q_CH12_025","node":"gr4_units","topicId":"ch12","subTopic":"Score, dozen, gross word problem","difficulty":"Hard","questionText":"A box contains 3 gross of pencils. If 5 dozen pencils are given away, how many pencils are left?","questionLatex":"3 \\text{ gross} - 5 \\text{ dozen} = ? \\text{ pencils}","options":[{"id":"A","text":"372"},{"id":"B","text":"432"},{"id":"C","text":"7"},{"id":"D","text":"31"}],"correctAnswer":"A","hints":["Convert everything to individual pencils. 1 gross = 144. 1 dozen = 12.","3 gross = 3 × 144 = 432 pencils. 5 dozen = 5 × 12 = 60 pencils.","432 - 60 = 372 pencils"],"stepByStep":[{"step":1,"text":"3 gross = 3 × 144 = 432 pencils","latex":"3 \\times 144 = 432"},{"step":2,"text":"5 dozen = 5 × 12 = 60 pencils","latex":"5 \\times 12 = 60"},{"step":3,"text":"Left = 432 - 60 = 372 pencils","latex":"\\boxed{432 - 60 = 372 \\text{ pencils}}"}],"misconceptions":{"A":"","B":"Forgot to subtract (this is the starting amount)","C":"Subtracted in dozens: 3 gross = 36 dozen, 36 - 5 = 31 (but forgot to convert back)","D":"Subtracted gross - dozen without converting: 36 - 5 = 31 dozens, not pencils"},"source":"hand_crafted"}
